<title>POLAND: Polish c.bank ups max 91-day bill yield to 22.50.</title>
<headline>Polish c.bank ups max 91-day bill yield to 22.50.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland raised the maximum yield of its 91-day bills by 0.2 point to 22.50 percent at the primary auction for money market dealers on Tuesday, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The average yield was 22.46 percent and the bank sold 207 million zlotys worth of the paper from a 400 million zloty offer after banks bid to buy 369 million zlotys of the bills.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
